Responsibilities
● Design and build advanced applications for the Android platform using Kotlin and
Jetpack Compose.
● Collaborate with cross-functional teams to define, design, and ship new features.
● Work with outside data sources and APIs (RESTful, GraphQL, Firebase, etc.).
● Unit-test code for robustness, including edge cases, usability, and general reliability.
● Work on bug fixing and improving application performance.
● Continuously discover, evaluate, and implement new technologies to maximize
development efficiency.
● Mentor junior developers and contribute to code reviews and technical documentation.
● Adhere to clean code and scalable architecture principles such as MVVM / MVI,
modularization, and clean architecture.
● Participate in the release process including Play Store deployment.

Requirements
● Bachelor’s/Master’s degree in Computer Science, Engineering, or a related field.
● 5-8 years of hands-on experience in Android app development.
● Proficient in Kotlin and experienced with Jetpack libraries (ViewModel, LiveData,
Navigation, Room, WorkManager).

● Strong understanding of Jetpack Compose and declarative UI patterns.
● Experience with Dependency Injection (Hilt/Dagger).
● Familiarity with architectural patterns like MVVM / MVI / Clean Architecture.
● Experience with Unit Testing and UI Testing frameworks (JUnit, Espresso, MockK).
● Experience integrating third-party SDKs (Firebase, Crashlytics, Analytics, etc.).
● Knowledge of CI/CD tools such as Bitrise, Jenkins, or GitHub Actions.
● Understanding of the full mobile development life cycle.
● Experience with Agile/Scrum methodologies.
● Excellent problem-solving skills and attention to detail.

Good to Have
● Exposure to modular app development and multi-module projects.
● Understanding of performance optimization and memory management in Android.
● Experience with Jetpack Compose animation and custom layouts.
● Familiarity with tools like SonarQube, Lint, or static analysis.
● Contribution to open-source projects or a strong GitHub portfolio.